markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Utilizing the Project Guide 

## What It Is: 
**The Project Guide is not a task list or a timeline.** Instead, it is a living document that captures student thinking, reasoning, and decisions as the project evolves over five specific milestones.

> #### While the final app shows what was built, the Project Guide explains the how and why.

<img src="https://images.code.org/3c574ded53b8358baff9d862f7c5df4a-image-1776697705188.png" alt="milestone one project guide" width="550px" style="border-radius:10px; float:right; margin: 0 0 40px 20px; box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.15);">

##What It Covers: 
The guide is divided into sections that mirror the project's milestones: 
- Intent & Scope (Day 1)
- System Explanation (Day 2)
- Testing & Behavior (Day 3+)
- Feedback & Iteration (Day 8)
- Final Reflection

<div style="clear:both;"></div>

## Keeping the Flow:

This document is designed for iteration. Students should not just fill it out once and forget it; they are explicitly instructed to revisit and add on to earlier sections whenever their ideas, scope, or system designs change based on testing or feedback

This ongoing documentation proves that their understanding is evolving.

---

## Using the Project Guide to Manage:

<!-- Pacing & Redirection -->
<div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 15px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
  <img src="https://images.code.org/a6383b704bd9c70435c6eb9c54f81352-image-1776699709862.png" alt="compass icon" style="width: 20%; max-width: 120px; height: auto; border-radius: 12px;">
  <div style="flex: 1; background: #f7f8fa; padding: 15px; border-radius: 10px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);">
    <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 10px;"><b>Pacing &amp; Redirection</b></h3>
    <p style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 10px;">If students are rushing to write code on Day 2, redirect them to the System Explanation section of the guide.</p>
    <p style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">Require them to clearly explain the flow of one user interaction (user action → app decision → user sees) before they are allowed to build.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Evidence for Grading -->
<div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 15px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
  <img src="https://images.code.org/f8904ce9bbd20f037eb7b5b6f701cc15-image-1776699786662.png" alt="clipboard icon" style="width: 20%; max-width: 120px; height: auto; border-radius: 12px;">
  <div style="flex: 1; background: #f7f8fa; padding: 15px; border-radius: 10px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);">
    <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 10px;"><b>Evidence for Grading</b></h3>
    <p style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">The guide is your primary artifact for grading the Project Planning &amp; Intentional Design and Responsible AI &amp; Ethical Reflection categories on the rubric.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Justifying Decisions -->
<div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 15px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
  <img src="https://images.code.org/e03c589871538d69ec74607fa153fb6a-image-1776699823913.png" alt="magnifying glass icon" style="width: 20%; max-width: 120px; height: auto; border-radius: 12px;">
  <div style="flex: 1; background: #f7f8fa; padding: 15px; border-radius: 10px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);">
    <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 10px;"><b>Justifying Decisions</b></h3>
    <p style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 10px;">Remind students that their reflections in the guide are evidence of their learning, not just busywork.</p>
    <p style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">Use the guide to push teams to justify why they changed a feature, rather than just listing what they changed.</p>
  </div>
</div>


MARKDOWN
